# Screenshots must not contain personal data

Every screenshot saved under `images/docs/` must be free of personal data BEFORE it is
written to the repo. Never commit a screenshot and fix it afterwards.

## What counts as personal data

- Email addresses
- Real names of people
- Account names and account IDs that identify a real account
- Phone numbers, IP addresses, API tokens, any credential

## How to remove it

Replace real values with placeholders in the page with JavaScript BEFORE the first capture.
Cropping is framing, not protection: the full screenshot must already be clean.

Build every placeholder from the real value as it is displayed: keep the same length,
separators, and prefix (a 7-digit ID becomes another 7-digit ID, a token shaped like `12345$`
plus hex keeps that shape). The same real value gets the same placeholder everywhere in one
article, and different values get different placeholders.

| Real data | Placeholder |
|---|---|
| Email address | `user@example.com`, then `user2@example.com` |
| Hostname, URL | same subdomains, registered part replaced: `cdn.resource1.example.com` |
| Public IPv4 | `203.0.113.10`, then `.11` (RFC 5737 documentation range) |
| IPv6 | `2001:db8::1` (RFC 3849) |
| Token, key, secret, numeric ID, UUID | the same shape as the real value |
| Person or account name | `my-account`, then `my-account-2` |

Private addresses (10.x, 172.16-31.x, 192.168.x) stay as they are.

The snippets and the full procedure are in `.claude/skills/article-screenshot/SKILL.md`.
Elements that only show the account (avatar menu, user block) may be hidden with
`visibility: hidden`. A blurred or pixelated real value is acceptable only when
replacement is impossible.

## Check before saving

Read the captured image back and scan it for real emails, names, IDs, tokens, and addresses. If any remain, retake the screenshot. Do not rely on a later manual edit.
